<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns $300 mln in put options.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns $300 mln in put options.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico said Monday it had placed all $300 million in dollar put options that it had offered for the month of June.</p>
<p>The options had an average premium of 20.61 pesos per $1,000.</p>
<p>Demand for the put options was $1.50 billion.</p>
<p>The central bank said in a statement that 16 institutions had placed bids. Five of these were assigned the options.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559))</p>
</text>
